 campaign in a deeply Democratic state.", "watch": "Only a major late scandal or sharply distorted turnout could narrow what polls consistently show as a roughly twenty-point Healey lead.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Maura Healey (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Massachusetts Governor Maura Healey seeks a second term against Republican Mike Minogue, with independent Andrea James also on the ballot. Polling throughout 2026 has shown Healey with a wide lead, and the latest surveys from Suffolk University and UMass Amherst put her advantage in the low-to-mid twenties. Every major race rating outlet calls the contest Solid or Safe Democratic.\n\nThe state's Democratic lean of about fourteen points, combined with Healey's incumbency and her steady polling position, leaves Minogue with a narrow path. His campaign has centered on affordability, but coverage notes Trump weighs on Republican prospects in Massachusetts, and a pro-Minogue super PAC has targeted the independent candidate rather than Healey. A Boston Globe column describes the race as one Healey was never in danger of losing. Prediction markets price her chances at roughly 96 percent, and the expected margin is around twenty points.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 18.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9921, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "